          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On December 20, 2011, at approximately 10:05 PM, a witness observed in the sky the straight and silent movement of a red object with lights in its center. This testimony describes the characteristics of Thai lanterns: orange-red balls moving with the wind (west wind, see weather report). The end-of-year holiday season may have been the reason for this modest release of a lantern. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of a Thai lantern.",
